A||||3||Splash||2.8 V6 Instalation
Z||000000||Splash||05-16-99||01:31 PM||||<br>I have an '85 2M4 5 speed and would like to install the factory V6 into this car, what major obsticles will I encounter, ECM/Exhaust/Fuel pump/Motor mounts?
Z||000001||PaUL||05-17-99||02:22 AM||||Splash,<br>The easyest way to go would be to get all the mounts, exhaust, ECM, wiring harness, and brackets from a donor Fiero, in fact the best thing to do would be to swap out the entire drivetrain cradle and all. If this is not available, you still can use your original transmission. Ive read that the Isuzu built 5spd in the 2m4 isnt strong enough to handle the V6 but it does bolt up to the 2.8 block. Im using an Isuzu trans with a 2.8 block, you just need to change the clutch to the larger diameter one that comes with the 2.8.
Z||000002||Lynx||05-17-99||02:53 AM||||From what i have heard and read its around the same price to replace the 4-cylinder with a V-8 as it is to replace it with a V-6. Unless you have a whole other car with a V-6 and got it cheap. I have the same car as you and plan to do a V-8 swap when the 4 blows up.
Z||000003||PaUL||05-17-99||09:32 PM||||I think it depends on what kind of V8 your putting in, a brand new V8 from a Corvette wouldnt be cheap.
